{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KvGvsjjQQpU1vUm94tsk35","type":"tool_result","content":"nt or model family until its reset: a job that stops at a subscription usage limit records the limit (in the controller database, so a restart keeps it), and the pool answers `limited` to any candidate whose role runs on that account or family (a whole-account session or weekly limit blocks every role; an Opus or Sonnet limit blocks only roles on that family, and a role with no model, which runs the CLI default, is blocked by any limit). A limited candidate takes no slot and reserves no demand, so lower classes are not held back. The block ends at the reset time the CLI reported; when it reported none the first pause is 30 minutes and each further stop with no reset doubles it up to 4 hours, starting over once a job succeeds; a reset time further away than 8 days is clamped. Running jobs are never killed for a limit. Deterministic scanners and the merger use no model and are unaffected.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d23dce7-d7be-43a4-888a-f4c7b737fbff","uuid":"b8dbfb5d-88bc-42ae-9a79-8dc53dacf01b","timestamp":"2026-11-23T18:44:21.164Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"nt or model family until its reset: a job that stops at a subscription usage limit records the limit (in the controller database, so a restart keeps it), and the pool answers `limited` to any candidate whose role runs on that account or family (a whole-account session or weekly limit blocks every role; an Opus or Sonnet limit blocks only roles on that family, and a role with no model, which runs the CLI default, is blocked by any limit). A limited candidate takes no slot and reserves no demand, so lower classes are not held back. The block ends at the reset time the CLI reported; when it reported none the first pause is 30 minutes and each further stop with no reset doubles it up to 4 hours, starting over once a job succeeds; a reset time further