{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLMWezXpZ2ZBuu1wHWzw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the daily dollar caps at the pool's claim gate, and `go test ./...` passes. `gofmt` and `go vet` are clean. The report is at `.ard/236/worker-engineer.md`.\n\n- **State:** migration `0007_budget.sql` adds an index on `step_usage.recorded_at`, and `SpendSince` sums today's spend per (stage, role) and for the whole repo.\n- **Gate:** the new `internal/budget` package refuses a candidate when `spent >= cap`. A read failure also refuses (fails closed). It logs `budget.capped` once per cap per UTC day. Reviewers get no exemption. Deterministic scanners are exempt.\n- **Pool:** it has a new `DeniedBudget` verdict that takes no slot, and a job that already holds a slot is untouched.\n- **Serve:** `adoptPool` takes the hook and `budget` is added to `knownLoops`.\n- **Docs:** I updated the Budgets, pool and Configuration text in `docs/proposal.md`, and added one Layout line to `CLAUDE.md`.\n- **Tests:** serve-level tests with a real store and fake clock cover:\n  - the role cap and the repo cap;\n  - a job that already holds a slot;\n  - a restart;\n  - the midnight reset;\n  - a read failure;\n  - `--loops budget`.\n\n  I also updated an existing schema-version test from 6 to 7.\n\nOpen points for you:\n- **Role caps:** a role with no cap of its own is limited only by the repo cap. That was the plan's assumption, and I couldn't check it against the parent design.\n- **`--loops budget`:** it is accepted but registers no loop, because the gate is always on in the pool.\n- **Status issue:** the status-issue post when a cap is hit is not implemented. The cap is only logged. The `docs/proposal.md` Budgets text no longer says it posts there.\n- **Approval:** `CLAUDE.md` is a protected path, so a human has to approve the PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage"